---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Responsible Gambling — Tools, Limits & Free UK Support"
  description="Free UK safer gambling tools explained: GamStop self-exclusion, deposit limits, reality checks and where to get confidential help. 18+."
>
  <article class="article-wrap">
    <h1>Responsible gambling</h1>
    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        Gambling should always be entertainment — never a way to make money or solve financial
        problems. This page lists the free tools and support services available to every UK
        player. All of them are confidential and most take only minutes to set up.
      </p>

      <h2>Free tools every UK player should know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong><a href="https://www.gamstop.co.uk" rel="noopener nofollow">GamStop</a></strong> —
          free national self-exclusion. One registration blocks you from every UKGC-licensed
          gambling site for 6 months, 1 year or 5 years.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deposit limits</strong> — every UKGC-licensed casino must let you set daily,
          weekly and monthly deposit limits. Set them before your first deposit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reality checks</strong> — on-screen reminders showing how long you've played
          and your net position.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Time-outs</strong> — short cooling-off periods (24 hours to 6 weeks) available
          at every licensed operator.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bank gambling blocks</strong> — most UK banks (Monzo, Starling, Barclays,
          Lloyds, HSBC and others) offer a free gambling transaction block in their app.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Signs that gambling may be becoming a problem</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Spending more time or money than you planned</li>
        <li>Chasing losses or gambling to escape stress</li>
        <li>Borrowing money to gamble, or hiding gambling from others</li>
        <li>Gambling affecting your work, sleep or relationships</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Free, confidential support</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>National Gambling Helpline:</strong> 0808 8020 133 (24/7, free) — run by
          <a href="https://www.gamcare.org.uk" rel="noopener nofollow">GamCare</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><a href="https://www.begambleaware.org" rel="noopener nofollow">BeGambleAware</a></strong> —
          free information, self-assessment and treatment referrals
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><a href="https://www.gamblersanonymous.org.uk" rel="noopener nofollow">Gamblers Anonymous UK</a></strong> —
          peer support meetings across the UK
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>NHS National Gambling Clinic</strong> — specialist treatment, referral via GP
          or self-referral
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout rg">
        <strong>Under 18?</strong> Gambling is illegal for anyone under 18 in the UK. If you're
        worried about your own or someone else's gambling, contact the National Gambling
        Helpline on 0808 8020 133 — it's free and confidential.
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
